# Revise the Analysis header layout

Remove the unfinished Graph action and restore a full-width Production/Plans selector, with Help aligned to the player selector below it.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The Graph button and its reserved layout space are removed from Analysis.
- [x] No Graph accessibility element or inactive Graph action remains.
- [x] The Production/Plans selector spans the available content width again.
- [x] Production and Plans retain clear, accessible selected states and existing tab-switching behavior.
- [x] The player selector remains directly beneath the Production/Plans selector.
- [x] The Analysis Help button appears at the right side of the player-selector row and is vertically aligned with it.
- [x] Help retains an independent, non-overlapping hit target and opens only the Analysis help content.
- [x] The revised two-row header fits supported compact iPhone widths without clipping or wrapping.
- [x] Existing player and All-player selection behavior remains unchanged.
- [x] SCR-002 is updated to describe the revised header before implementation is completed.
- [x] UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused layout and interaction checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Scope notes

- This task supersedes TASK-035's compact selector and same-row Graph/Help layout.
- Adding a replacement graph entry point is out of scope.

## Evidence

- Removed the Graph action and its accessibility/layout elements.
- Restored the selector to the padded full content width and placed Help at the far right of the player row.
- Updated SCR-002 and UI assertions for full-width layout, vertical alignment, and Graph absence.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
